anyr claude — launch Claude Code through AnyRouter

Usage:
  anyr claude [options] [claude flags and args] [-- <raw claude args>]

Launches the coding agent through AnyRouter (signs in first if needed).

Options:
  --yes, --ok           Skip confirmation prompts (login / install)
  --model auto|<id>     Session model. auto / anyrouter/auto; [1m] and [500k] are min-context floors on auto (not catalog SKUs).
  --haiku <id>          Claude /model haiku and subagents
  --sonnet <id>         Claude /model sonnet
  --opus <id>           Claude /model opus
  --fable <id>          Claude /model fable (also the auto-fallback target)
  --preset <slug>       Launch with your saved preset (model @preset/<slug>); fails
                        if it does not exist. Cannot be combined with --model
  --hub <slug>          Load a hub: sync ~/.anyrouter/hubs + claude --plugin-dir
  --profile <name>      Use a named profile
  --command-path <path> Explicit path to the agent executable
  --install             Install a missing agent without prompting (implied on a TTY)
  --config <path>       Override the config file path
  --dry-run             Print the child command and env (secrets redacted);
                        with --json, the plan as one JSON object
  --json                anyr's own output as JSON; never sent to the agent
                        (for the agent's own --json, put it after `--`)
  --no-mcp              Don't connect the AnyRouter MCP gateway (or its
                        artifact tools) this launch
                        (`anyr mcp auto off` turns it off on this machine)
  --device              Force the device-code flow (headless / SSH)
  --device-code         Alias of --device
  --paste               Force the paste-a-key flow, skipping auto-detection

Portable flags (one name on every agent; anyr passes the agent's own flag):
  --yolo                Skip permission prompts; passes --dangerously-skip-permissions
  --effort <level>      Reasoning effort: minimal | low | medium | high | xhigh | max; sets MAX_THINKING_TOKENS
  --print               Answer the prompt that follows it without the UI, then exit; passes -p
  --continue            Continue the most recent session; passes --continue
  --resume [<id>]       Resume a session by id; with no id, the agent's own picker or latest; passes --resume <id>
  --system <text>       Replace the system prompt; passes --system-prompt <text>
  --append-system <text> Add text to the default system prompt; passes --append-system-prompt <text>
  --add-dir <path>      Let the agent use one more directory (repeatable); passes --add-dir <path>
  --cwd <path>          No effect: Claude Code has no working-directory flag
  --max-turns <n>       Stop after this many agent turns; passes --max-turns <n> (hidden from --help)
  --no-tools, --tools-off Start with every built-in tool off; passes --tools=
  --no-skills, --skills-off Do not load skills; passes --disable-slash-commands

Any other flag goes to the agent unchanged and in order, no `--` needed:
  anyr claude --model <id> --verbose
Everything after `--` goes to the agent raw, including flags anyr also owns.

First run with no config auto-detects the best way to sign in — browser first,
falling back to the device-code flow automatically.

